{
  "_readme": "Tunable game balance. Edit this, re-zip the .xdc, done \u2014 no code changes needed for anything in here. Each top-level section (world, classes, revive, downed, waves, hive, aliens) is used as a whole: if you define a section here it fully replaces that default section (e.g. redefine 'classes' with your own roster and the built-in Officer/Specialist/Medic won't linger), and any section you leave out entirely just keeps its default. 'behavior' fields pick from a fixed set of movement/targeting strategies implemented in the game (see _behaviors below); they are not custom code. Wire-protocol numeric alien 'type' ids (0-4) must stay attached to the same archetype across everyone using this build, since peers only exchange numbers, not this file.",
  "_behaviors": {
    "chase": "Walks straight at whichever living player is currently nearest.",
    "chaseAndTrail": "Same as chase, but periodically drops a lingering damage patch behind it.",
    "rushAndDetonate": "Chases like normal until within triggerRadius, then arms (flashes) for fuseFrames and explodes.",
    "flee": "Moves directly away from the nearest living player instead of toward them."
  },
